{#-
  data-form="updates" — email updates capture.

  While features.formsOpen is false NO input, checkbox or submit button is
  rendered: only the message. That is deliberate (design-source/README.md §5) —
  a visually dimmed form is still keyboard-focusable and submittable, which
  fails WCAG.

  When open (records/changes/CHG-009) it posts to the same-origin handler
  /api/signup/updates (website/functions/api/signup/updates.js), which forwards
  to the uncost-signups Worker; that sends a 7-day confirmation link (double
  opt-in). With JS on, ui.js sends it with fetch and writes the result into
  the note; with JS off, the browser lands on /updates/check-email/ (or
  /signup/not-sent/). The consent and age boxes are required and unticked;
  their texts come from _data/signups.json, which the handler hashes into the
  consent event. hp_url is a honeypot.

  The form appears twice on the homepage and on /join/ (in the page and in
  the footer), so its ids carry the surface: footer.njk sets
  updatesSurface = "footer"; elsewhere it follows the page.
-#}
{% if features.formsOpen %}
{%- set upSurface = updatesSurface or ("home" if page.url == "/" else ("join" if page.url == "/join/" else "page")) %}
<div data-updates-form>
  <form class="ft-form" data-form="updates" data-live action="/api/signup/updates" method="post">
    <label class="skip-link" for="up-{{ upSurface }}-email">Email address</label>
    <input id="up-{{ upSurface }}-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email" maxlength="254" required>
    <button type="submit">Get updates</button>
    <input type="hidden" name="surface" value="{{ upSurface }}">
    <div class="hp" hidden><label for="up-{{ upSurface }}-hp">Leave this field empty</label><input id="up-{{ upSurface }}-hp" type="text" name="hp_url" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></div>
    <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="consent" value="yes" required><span>{{ signups.texts.email_updates }} <a href="/privacy/#s11">Privacy policy</a></span></label>
    <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="age" value="yes" required><span>{{ signups.texts.age | replace("{minAge}", signups.minAge) }}</span></label>
  </form>
  <div class="ft-note" data-updates-note role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
</div>
{% else %}
<div data-updates-form data-form="updates" class="form-off">
  <div class="form-off-msg">Sign-ups open soon.</div>
  <div class="form-off-sub">The updates list opens soon. Nothing to enter yet.</div>
</div>
{% endif %}
